<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Escuela Politécnica Nacional</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1869">1869</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Escuela Politécnica Nacional is a public university of engineering and science in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quito">Quito</a>, founded in 1869 by President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gabriel-garcia-moreno">Gabriel García Moreno</a>. He brought German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> scientists to teach there, making it a centre of scientific study in Ecuador. After his death it was closed for a time, and it was re-established in 1935; it remains one of the country's leading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/technical-university">technical universities</a>.</p></div>
